WEBVTT

00:02:00.290 --> 00:02:04.290
Let's build a house

00:02:07.160 --> 00:02:08.290
What happened here?

00:02:35.040 --> 00:02:36.110
Menori...

00:02:46.390 --> 00:02:47.470
What a relief...

00:02:53.320 --> 00:02:56.380
The shuttle's smashed to bits,
and she's worried about her violin?

00:02:56.660 --> 00:02:59.100
That's true, but who broke the shuttle?

00:03:02.960 --> 00:03:03.820
Look!

00:03:06.640 --> 00:03:07.780
This is...

00:03:09.730 --> 00:03:12.710
...the monster. It was that monster!

00:03:13.310 --> 00:03:15.350
Then the one who broke the shuttle...

00:03:16.140 --> 00:03:16.720
Hey!

00:03:17.020 --> 00:03:18.020
What are we going to do?

00:03:18.520 --> 00:03:20.300
We have no place to sleep and no fire!

00:03:20.640 --> 00:03:22.950
The fire watch was your job, wasn't it?

00:03:31.950 --> 00:03:33.220
We made it in time somehow.

00:03:34.200 --> 00:03:36.340
Alright! Way to go. Bell!

00:03:36.770 --> 00:03:38.660
You're in a good mood, all things considered.

00:03:45.040 --> 00:03:46.400
Camp here?

00:03:46.690 --> 00:03:48.950
That monster might still be nearby!

00:03:49.630 --> 00:03:51.130
We can't move at night...

00:03:51.580 --> 00:03:54.600
...so we'll take turns at watch
and spend tonight here.

00:03:55.180 --> 00:03:56.170
"Tonight?"

00:03:56.900 --> 00:04:00.490
It'd be better to leave here
and move to The Great Tree.

00:04:06.110 --> 00:04:07.760
Now that we've lost the shuttle...

00:04:08.270 --> 00:04:09.540
...it's not safe here anymore.

00:04:10.090 --> 00:04:11.450
We have no choice but to build a house.

00:04:11.700 --> 00:04:13.370
Shingo! When can we have it done?

00:04:13.820 --> 00:04:16.800
If Howard doesn't interfere, pretty soon.

00:04:17.250 --> 00:04:18.410
What?

00:04:18.520 --> 00:04:19.250
Stop it.

00:04:20.140 --> 00:04:23.270
Anyways, we all have to cooperate
and build it quickly.

00:04:23.770 --> 00:04:27.600
We'll have to get a lot more logs
ready to make into the floor.

00:04:27.970 --> 00:04:30.170
And the ones this time were too weak.

00:04:30.410 --> 00:04:33.560
It's gonna take a lot more time.

00:04:40.850 --> 00:04:41.660
Hey...

00:04:41.660 --> 00:04:42.950
...instead of logs...

00:04:42.950 --> 00:04:44.300
...maybe we can use those.

00:04:49.140 --> 00:04:50.400
Those would be plenty sturdy.

00:04:50.960 --> 00:04:52.820
It won't take as long as cutting timber, either.

00:04:53.250 --> 00:04:54.940
Right? It's a good idea, isn't it?

00:04:57.040 --> 00:04:58.390
I dunno...

00:04:58.800 --> 00:04:59.660
Why not?

00:05:00.280 --> 00:05:01.570
Isn't it a good idea?

00:05:02.270 --> 00:05:04.740
It was a good idea to have made
Luna the leader after all.

00:05:05.680 --> 00:05:07.800
Alright! First thing tomorrow...

00:05:07.800 --> 00:05:08.620
Wait a minute.

00:05:11.290 --> 00:05:14.080
How do you plan to move those wings?

00:05:16.540 --> 00:05:18.750
Yeah, that's a real problem.

00:05:19.220 --> 00:05:23.900
With everyone here dragging it,
we barely changed its position.

00:05:24.730 --> 00:05:26.900
Come to think of it, that's true.

00:05:28.500 --> 00:05:29.870
It was too soon to be happy.

00:05:30.240 --> 00:05:33.450
Your careless talk caused disappointment for everyone.

00:05:33.690 --> 00:05:34.760
It lowered our morale.

00:05:35.400 --> 00:05:37.090
That's the worst thing a leader can do.

00:05:37.670 --> 00:05:39.800
You didn't hafta say it that way!

00:05:40.820 --> 00:05:41.660
Sorry...

00:05:44.300 --> 00:05:46.910
They're just right for the floor, though.

00:05:59.640 --> 00:06:00.800
It's time to get moving.

00:06:11.020 --> 00:06:12.000
What are you doing?

00:06:14.210 --> 00:06:16.270
There's a lot we might be able to use.

00:06:16.460 --> 00:06:17.400
For example...

00:06:19.370 --> 00:06:20.170
This.

00:06:21.670 --> 00:06:23.000
If we do this...

00:06:23.320 --> 00:06:25.160
It becomes a pulley.

00:06:30.600 --> 00:06:32.120
And this window...

00:06:32.940 --> 00:06:34.270
...can be put in the house too.

00:06:35.790 --> 00:06:37.610
I'm going to use this!

00:06:37.610 --> 00:06:38.700
Can you carry it?

00:06:41.920 --> 00:06:44.250
I'll definitely carry it!

00:06:45.640 --> 00:06:46.540
It's impossible.

00:06:47.360 --> 00:06:48.470
What's this?

00:06:49.070 --> 00:06:50.890
Leaves from The Great Tree.

00:06:51.220 --> 00:06:52.420
Do what you want with them.

00:06:53.680 --> 00:06:54.690
Don't need 'em.

00:07:00.430 --> 00:07:01.650
What are you doing?

00:07:03.390 --> 00:07:04.760
I'm taking the embers.

00:07:05.250 --> 00:07:06.170
If we have these...

00:07:06.670 --> 00:07:08.660
...we can start a fire over there as well.

00:07:16.180 --> 00:07:18.350
Somehow, it seems like a waste.

00:07:19.740 --> 00:07:21.280
If we don't put it out properly...

00:07:21.500 --> 00:07:23.550
...it could start a fire, which would be a problem.

00:07:45.320 --> 00:07:49.670
That's a lot of trouble.
Isn't there an easier way to start a fire?

00:07:51.450 --> 00:07:54.410
If it goes out, we'll just get
Bell to start another one.

00:07:59.720 --> 00:08:03.020
Kaoru and I will look for strong logs and vines.

00:08:04.910 --> 00:08:05.790
We're counting on you.

00:08:06.150 --> 00:08:09.190
In the meantime, we'll be setting up pulleys with Shingo.

00:08:09.900 --> 00:08:10.650
Alright!

00:08:11.210 --> 00:08:13.140
Well, I'll take responsibility for the fire...

00:08:13.140 --> 00:08:13.800
Here.

00:08:14.040 --> 00:08:16.420
Menori and Howard, take care of food, please.

00:08:35.940 --> 00:08:37.160
That feels good.

00:08:39.170 --> 00:08:40.500
It's true.

00:08:41.490 --> 00:08:46.090
An invigorating wind, the smell of the lake,
and the sound of the rustling leaves...

00:08:58.140 --> 00:08:59.080
Run away!

00:09:11.740 --> 00:09:13.050
Luna!

00:09:14.000 --> 00:09:15.500
It's super big.

00:09:15.790 --> 00:09:16.930
What is it?

00:09:55.850 --> 00:09:57.070
Ouch!

00:10:37.820 --> 00:10:39.040
It's okay now.

00:10:39.770 --> 00:10:40.890
You're okay.

00:10:43.050 --> 00:10:44.590
What happened?

00:11:14.270 --> 00:11:16.070
So you like these leaves.

00:11:18.750 --> 00:11:19.350
Here.

00:11:26.850 --> 00:11:28.200
You want more?

00:11:29.770 --> 00:11:31.690
Hey! Look, look!

00:11:31.690 --> 00:11:34.220
I caught them! You should...

00:11:38.700 --> 00:11:41.920
<i>Papa!</i>

00:11:41.920 --> 00:11:45.050
Wait! It's okay!

00:11:59.320 --> 00:12:00.300
Are you okay?

00:12:31.630 --> 00:12:33.320
You can't take risks like that.

00:12:33.690 --> 00:12:36.410
That monster could smash you easily!

00:12:36.560 --> 00:12:37.930
It's not a monster!

00:12:38.620 --> 00:12:40.480
And you only say that because its body is big...

00:12:40.760 --> 00:12:43.160
...when it's really a gentle creature.

00:12:44.230 --> 00:12:46.800
But it's a fact that it attacked the shuttle.

00:12:47.340 --> 00:12:49.970
That's because it wanted
the leaves from The Great Tree.

00:12:50.230 --> 00:12:53.150
Then it could have eaten them
quietly and gone home, right?

00:12:53.300 --> 00:12:56.450
But it got a piece of the shuttle stuck in its side...

00:12:56.450 --> 00:12:57.670
That again?

00:12:58.090 --> 00:13:01.390
And I suppose it said, "Pull it out please!"

00:13:02.060 --> 00:13:04.160
I got a feeling like it was saying just that.

00:13:05.920 --> 00:13:08.870
It certainly didn't try to attack me!

00:13:09.320 --> 00:13:10.930
Right? You all saw.

00:13:11.100 --> 00:13:13.200
It didn't seem all that gentle to me.

00:13:13.500 --> 00:13:14.700
I was scared too.

00:13:15.950 --> 00:13:16.890
And Sharla?

00:13:20.750 --> 00:13:23.720
Even if it seems gentle, it's a feral beast.

00:13:26.190 --> 00:13:29.750
You're safe because I shouted and chased it away.

00:13:30.200 --> 00:13:33.490
Only an idiot'd run away when it heard Howard scream.

00:13:35.440 --> 00:13:37.460
We're camping until the house is finished.

00:13:38.320 --> 00:13:40.220
It may come again during that time.

00:13:40.890 --> 00:13:42.220
I can't get that out of my mind.

00:13:42.220 --> 00:13:45.040
If only we had the wings of the shuttle...

00:13:45.880 --> 00:13:50.720
If that monster's really so nice,
why don't you ask it to carry them?

00:13:52.870 --> 00:13:54.390
I think it definitely would!

00:13:58.090 --> 00:13:59.870
Hey! Are you serious?

00:14:00.350 --> 00:14:01.180
Luna...

00:14:05.790 --> 00:14:07.590
If it goes into a rage...

00:14:08.810 --> 00:14:11.510
...it would put everyone in danger.

00:14:13.090 --> 00:14:14.290
You're right.

00:14:14.790 --> 00:14:16.010
I should just forget it.

00:14:19.120 --> 00:14:20.660
Anyways, let's go to sleep.

00:14:21.130 --> 00:14:22.970
We'll be busy again tomorrow.

00:14:23.400 --> 00:14:24.900
If you sleep in, we'll leave you behind!

00:14:25.220 --> 00:14:26.830
Good night.

00:14:27.070 --> 00:14:28.390
Good night, everyone.

00:14:37.070 --> 00:14:39.170
Bell, keep it at my pace!

00:14:39.430 --> 00:14:42.300
We still haven't cut down a single one! Let's speed up!

00:14:42.300 --> 00:14:44.100
Stop acting so full of yourself!

00:14:46.870 --> 00:14:48.640
It's okay like that, right?

00:15:17.470 --> 00:15:18.940
Finally got one?

00:15:19.480 --> 00:15:21.320
Don't just watch, help!

00:15:26.100 --> 00:15:28.330
I wonder if Bell and the rest
of them are making progress.

00:15:28.840 --> 00:15:32.340
I had Menori and Howard help him,
so they should be fine.

00:15:38.230 --> 00:15:39.650
Stay here. I'll get it.

00:16:44.980 --> 00:16:46.950
Th-- that's a relief.

00:16:48.130 --> 00:16:48.900
Thank you.

00:16:52.630 --> 00:16:55.270
Luna! Sharla!

00:16:59.870 --> 00:17:00.540
Were you watching?

00:17:01.090 --> 00:17:03.650
Yes. I still can't feel at ease...

00:17:04.370 --> 00:17:06.430
...but it seems gentle towards you.

00:17:09.000 --> 00:17:10.610
But it's certainly large.

00:17:11.270 --> 00:17:13.990
It seems like it might be able to lend us a hand.

00:17:22.350 --> 00:17:24.880
Sorry for making you do something like this.

00:17:25.120 --> 00:17:26.420
So big...

00:17:26.740 --> 00:17:28.400
It's actually listenin' to what we're sayin'.

00:17:37.350 --> 00:17:38.380
Are you full?

00:17:49.500 --> 00:17:50.640
What's up with that?

00:17:51.050 --> 00:17:52.140
Well, let's go.

00:17:53.790 --> 00:17:55.480
Leave the orders to me.

00:17:55.930 --> 00:17:57.220
Let's go, monster.

00:17:57.710 --> 00:17:58.350
Move!

00:17:59.000 --> 00:18:01.610
Mo~ve!

00:18:03.690 --> 00:18:05.550
That's right, move!

00:18:05.830 --> 00:18:07.370
Ah, you're coming this way!

00:18:07.870 --> 00:18:09.170
Pull them forward.

00:18:09.600 --> 00:18:13.100
Idiot, not behind you! What do you think you're doing?

00:18:13.100 --> 00:18:13.460
Stop!

00:18:13.460 --> 00:18:15.620
All you have to do is use your strength.

00:18:15.620 --> 00:18:16.720
Thinking is...

00:18:16.720 --> 00:18:18.050
Howard, shut up!

00:18:20.420 --> 00:18:21.390
Calm down.

00:18:23.850 --> 00:18:25.480
Over here! This way!

00:18:26.150 --> 00:18:26.920
This way.

00:18:31.800 --> 00:18:33.130
It's okay now.

00:18:40.930 --> 00:18:42.190
Okay, let's go.

00:18:58.690 --> 00:19:00.520
It worked! It moved!

00:19:03.620 --> 00:19:06.940
Because Howard acted so stupidly,
it's dented all over.

00:19:07.330 --> 00:19:10.200
But it saved us the trouble of flattening the wings.

00:19:10.480 --> 00:19:11.920
It's all thanks to me.

00:19:11.920 --> 00:19:13.220
It was coincidence!

00:19:21.490 --> 00:19:24.150
It'll be over soon, so bear with it.

00:19:29.290 --> 00:19:30.990
It's got a weird groan.

00:19:31.160 --> 00:19:32.720
It's ticklish.

00:19:36.730 --> 00:19:39.240
Pague... you're Pague, okay?

00:19:40.010 --> 00:19:41.250
Pague?

00:19:41.900 --> 00:19:43.100
That's a name?

00:19:44.020 --> 00:19:46.090
It's a calm and gentle...

00:19:46.740 --> 00:19:48.450
...and cute name, isn't it?

00:19:48.790 --> 00:19:49.950
Pague...

00:19:50.900 --> 00:19:52.140
Pague, huh?

00:19:54.090 --> 00:19:55.090
It might be perfect.

00:19:56.380 --> 00:19:58.480
Nice to meet you, Pague.

00:19:58.840 --> 00:20:01.520
"Pague"? You gotta be kiddin'.

00:20:01.950 --> 00:20:05.000
Hey, is that okay? Pague?

00:20:05.980 --> 00:20:07.090
Isn't it great?

00:20:07.460 --> 00:20:11.340
That we could meet it again,
and become such good friends.

00:20:19.480 --> 00:20:22.500
Yeah, that's good. Just keep pulling like that!

00:20:22.500 --> 00:20:23.590
It's amazing!

00:20:28.800 --> 00:20:30.920
That's good, keep going!

00:20:31.480 --> 00:20:32.290
Keep trying!

00:20:34.270 --> 00:20:35.490
--Alright.
--It lifted!

00:20:36.050 --> 00:20:37.820
It rose! It lifted up!

00:20:38.400 --> 00:20:39.470
Yeah, like that!

00:20:39.970 --> 00:20:40.990
--That's good.
--A little more!

00:20:40.990 --> 00:20:42.470
More, more!

00:20:55.370 --> 00:20:57.520
It seems like this is Pague's limit!

00:20:57.880 --> 00:20:58.870
It's a little further.

00:20:59.340 --> 00:21:00.450
Get it to continue.

00:21:00.710 --> 00:21:01.890
Don't ask for the impossible!

00:21:12.520 --> 00:21:13.330
Pague...

00:21:14.150 --> 00:21:15.820
We're countin' on you, Pague.

00:21:16.120 --> 00:21:17.820
Pague, please!

00:21:30.800 --> 00:21:32.740
Pague! A little more!

00:21:48.920 --> 00:21:50.440
It's up, it's up!

00:21:52.240 --> 00:21:53.340
It's over.

00:21:55.460 --> 00:21:56.620
You did it!

00:21:56.740 --> 00:21:57.750
Pague!

00:21:58.740 --> 00:21:59.980
Thank you!

00:22:01.650 --> 00:22:03.560
It's finally done, thanks to you.

00:22:09.800 --> 00:22:11.550
Pague, thank you.

00:22:11.870 --> 00:22:12.860
You really helped us.

00:22:13.630 --> 00:22:15.490
Nicely done, Pague.

00:22:15.650 --> 00:22:18.880
You've really turned into Pague now.

00:22:28.540 --> 00:22:30.490
Bye, Pague.

00:22:31.370 --> 00:22:33.640
If you get hungry, stop by anytime!

00:22:34.370 --> 00:22:37.540
Even on this planet, there are tame creatures.

00:22:39.240 --> 00:22:41.250
It's like our number of friends has grown.

00:22:42.190 --> 00:22:45.130
Our ninth companion...

00:22:45.950 --> 00:22:47.750
Companion?

00:23:02.810 --> 00:23:04.850
I am Menori Visconti.

00:23:06.190 --> 00:23:10.250
I was raised never to show weakness by my father, a member of the Space Commonwealth parliament.

00:23:10.850 --> 00:23:12.820
My heart closed before I noticed.

00:23:14.400 --> 00:23:16.760
But my life on this island...

00:23:17.300 --> 00:23:18.970
...and the time I've spent with my friends...

00:23:19.820 --> 00:23:21.600
...and the words she said...

00:23:22.030 --> 00:23:24.600
...returned me to my true form.

00:23:25.650 --> 00:23:28.220
Next time: Gentle Melody
